  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When angle of prism is small, then angle of deviation\r\n\r\nis given by $\\mathrm{D}_{\\mathrm{m}}=(\\mu-1) \\mathrm{A}$\r\n\r\nSo, if wavelength of incident light is increased, $\\mu$ decreases\r\n\r\nand hence $\\mathrm{D}_{\\mathrm{m}}$ decreases.",
    "image": null
